{
  "_README": "Each agent's CONNECTION: the harness it runs in, the key it runs on, its model (Harness and Keys on the observatory's Agents tab writes this file; docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-harness-and-keys-design.md). `*` is everyone else: an agent with no entry of its own runs on it, and with neither, on the org's own login. `credential` names a key in credentials.json (whose value is in .env, never here); `harness` a row of src/astryx/data/cli_adapters.json (default claude); `model` the model it runs, over its charter's Model:; `models` maps the harness's tier aliases for this agent; `effort` its effort level. Takes effect at the agent's next start. An older entry with base_url + token_env (the NAME of an .env key) still works.",

  "*": {
    "credential": "Work account"
  },

  "example-agent-on-deepseek": {
    "harness": "claude",
    "credential": "DeepSeek",
    "model": "deepseek-chat",
    "effort": "high"
  }
}
